export const additions = [
  {name:"Creamy Tomato Chicken Penne",category:"Family",tags:["Family","High Protein"],time:35,cost:1.76,protein:39,calories:668,difficulty:"Easy",score:9.5,emoji:"🍝",image:"/recipes/creamy-tomato-chicken-penne.jpg",blurb:"Golden chicken, tomato, crème fraîche and spinach wrapped round penne. Proper dinner, not a jar-sauce crime scene.",verdict:"Creamy enough to feel indulgent, sensible enough to make again next week.",ingredients:["300g chicken breast fillets","300g penne pasta","400g chopped tomatoes","300g crème fraîche","1 red onion","3 garlic cloves","100g baby spinach","100g grated hard cheese","1 tsp Italian herbs","1 tbsp olive oil","Salt and black pepper"],steps:["Get a large pan of salted water boiling and cook the penne until just tender. Drain it, save a splash of the water and stop it turning into wallpaper paste.","Cut the chicken into bite-sized pieces, season with salt, pepper and Italian herbs, then fry in hot olive oil for 5–6 minutes until golden and cooked through. Remove it before you dry it out for sport.","In the same pan, soften the onion for 2–3 minutes, then add the garlic for 30 seconds. Burn garlic and the whole kitchen will know you lost focus.","Pour in the tomatoes and simmer for 5 minutes until the sharp raw edge has gone. Let them actually bubble; warm tinned tomatoes are not yet a sauce.","Turn the heat down, stir in the crème fraîche, chicken, penne and spinach. Loosen with a little pasta water until the sauce coats everything instead of sitting in a puddle. Add it gradually; rescuing thick sauce is easier than rescuing soup.","Top with grated cheese and serve while it is glossy and hot. Add chilli flakes if bland food has been running your life."]},
  {name:"Chicken Chipolata One-Pan Lasagne",category:"Family",tags:["Family","One Pan"],time:45,cost:2.22,protein:36,calories:690,difficulty:"Easy",score:9.4,emoji:"🍲",image:"/recipes/chicken-chipolata-one-pan-lasagne.jpg",blurb:"Chicken chipolatas, broken lasagne sheets and bubbling cheese in one pan. Lasagne without the washing-up hostage situation.",verdict:"A proper cheesy bowlful with none of the faff of building sixteen layers.",ingredients:["10 chicken chipolata sausages","1 onion","1 tbsp tomato purée","1 tbsp mixed herbs","400g chopped tomatoes","400ml water","1 chicken stock pot","40ml balsamic vinegar","180g lasagne sheets","55g mozzarella and cheddar mix","30g grated hard cheese","120g cottage cheese","30g light cream cheese","40ml skimmed milk","10g parmesan","Salt and black pepper"],steps:["Remove the sausage skins if you fancy it, then brown the chipolatas with the onion in a wide pan. Get colour on them; pale sausage is just anxiety in a casing.","Stir through the tomato purée and mixed herbs for a minute so they wake up, then add tomatoes, water, stock pot and balsamic vinegar. Stir the stock pot in until it dissolves; nobody wants to bite into concentrated stock.","Snap the lasagne sheets into rough quarters and push them into the sauce. Stir every few minutes or they will glue themselves together out of spite.","Simmer for 15–20 minutes until the pasta is tender and the sauce has thickened. Separate the sheets as you stir; a glued-up stack stays hard in the middle.","Blend the cottage cheese, cream cheese, milk, parmesan, salt and pepper until smooth. This is your white sauce, not an excuse to make a washing-up mountain.","Spoon over the white sauce, scatter on both cheeses and grill until golden and bubbling. Leave it two minutes before eating unless you enjoy molten-cheese burns."]},
  {name:"Sticky Honey Garlic Chicken Rice Bowls",category:"High Protein",tags:["High Protein","Quick"],time:25,cost:2.18,protein:43,calories:638,difficulty:"Easy",score:9.6,emoji:"🍚",image:"/recipes/sticky-honey-garlic-chicken-rice-bowls.jpg",blurb:"Glossy honey-garlic chicken, rice, broccoli and carrot. Better than a takeaway bowl and you know what actually went in it.",verdict:"Sticky, savoury and fast enough for a weeknight with zero patience left.",ingredients:["450g chicken breasts","250g microwave rice","180g broccoli","1 carrot","2 garlic cloves","2 tbsp soy sauce","1½ tbsp honey","1 tsp ginger paste","1 tsp sesame seeds","2 spring onions","1 tsp cornflour","Salt and black pepper"],steps:["Slice the chicken into even bites and toss with cornflour, salt and pepper. Uneven chunks mean one bit is raw while another has become furniture.","Mix soy, honey, garlic and ginger in a bowl before the pan is hot. Trying to measure honey while chicken burns is amateur hour.","Pan-fry the chicken for 8–10 minutes until golden and cooked through, giving it space to brown instead of steaming. A crowded pan makes wet chicken, not a sear.","Microwave the rice and steam the broccoli until tender but still green. Grey broccoli has suffered enough.","Pour the sauce into the chicken pan and cook for 1–2 minutes until it turns thick, glossy and properly sticky. Keep it moving; honey burns faster than you can say takeaway.","Slice or grate the carrot and slice the spring onions, then build bowls with rice, broccoli, carrot and chicken. Fine carrot strips give crunch; enormous raw chunks just get in the way. Finish with sesame seeds and spring onion before it disappears."]},
  {name:"BBQ Beef Quesadillas",category:"Fakeaway",tags:["Quick","Family"],time:22,cost:2.08,protein:34,calories:704,difficulty:"Easy",score:9.4,emoji:"🌮",image:"/recipes/bbq-beef-quesadillas.jpg",blurb:"Smoky beef, sweetcorn and molten cheddar pressed inside crisp wraps. Napkins are not optional.",verdict:"Crunchy outside, properly messy inside. Exactly what a quesadilla is supposed to be.",ingredients:["350g beef mince","2 large wraps","60g reduced-fat cheddar","2 tbsp BBQ sauce","80g sweetcorn","¼ red onion","4 tbsp salsa","2 tbsp 0% Greek yoghurt","1 tsp garlic powder","1 tsp smoked paprika","½ tsp salt","¼ tsp black pepper"],steps:["Brown the mince in a hot frying pan, breaking it up well. Grey clumps are not a texture anyone requested.","Stir in BBQ sauce, garlic powder, smoked paprika, salt and pepper, then add the sweetcorn for one more minute. Let the sauce coat the mince before filling the wraps; loose liquid leaks straight out.","Spread the beef over one half of each wrap, leaving a border so the filling does not make a run for it.","Scatter over cheddar and finely chopped red onion, then fold the wraps shut firmly. Keep the filling on one half; overstuffing is how a quesadilla becomes a mess in the pan.","Toast in a dry frying pan for 2–3 minutes per side until the wraps are crisp and the cheese is properly melted. Lower the heat if the wrap browns too fast; a burnt tortilla with cold cheese is not a win.","Slice into wedges and serve with salsa and yoghurt. Give them a minute first; the filling is basically lava."]},
  {name:"Creamy Sausage Pasta Bake",category:"Family",tags:["Family","Budget"],time:45,cost:1.98,protein:31,calories:682,difficulty:"Easy",score:9.3,emoji:"🧀",image:"/recipes/creamy-sausage-pasta-bake.jpg",blurb:"Sausage, passata, spinach and a mozzarella lid that means business.",verdict:"Cheap, filling and bubbling at the edges like a proper family pasta bake should be.",ingredients:["6 sausages","250g pasta","300g passata","120g soft cheese","80g spinach","125g mozzarella","1 onion","2 garlic cloves","1 tsp olive oil","1 tsp mixed herbs","1 tsp paprika","Salt and black pepper"],steps:["Cook the pasta two minutes short of the packet time. It is going in the oven later, so do not boil all the life out of it now.","Remove the sausage meat from the skins and brown it hard with the onion. A little colour here carries the whole dish.","Add garlic, paprika and mixed herbs for 30 seconds, then stir in passata and soft cheese over a lower heat.","Fold in the spinach until wilted, then add the drained pasta and season properly. Fold it through until every tube has sauce, not just the first serving.","Tip into a baking dish, tear over the mozzarella and bake at 200°C for 15–18 minutes until bubbling and golden.","Rest for five minutes so it stops being a cheese avalanche, then serve hot."]},
  {name:"Sticky Pork Noodle Stir Fry",category:"Quick",tags:["Quick","High Protein"],time:25,cost:2.34,protein:37,calories:646,difficulty:"Easy",score:9.4,emoji:"🥢",image:"/recipes/sticky-pork-noodle-stir-fry.jpg",blurb:"Glossy pork, noodles and crunchy vegetables with enough sweet heat to keep things interesting.",verdict:"Fast, sticky and not remotely the limp noodle situation you were expecting.",ingredients:["400g pork strips","250g egg noodles","1 bell pepper","100g sugar snap peas","1 carrot","3 spring onions","2 garlic cloves","2 tbsp soy sauce","1 tbsp honey","1 tsp sesame oil","1 tsp ginger","½ tsp chilli flakes","Salt and black pepper"],steps:["Cook the noodles, drain them and rinse briefly so they do not weld themselves into one sad lump.","Season and sear the pork in a hot pan until browned. Do it in batches if the pan is small; steam is not a sear.","Slice the pepper, carrot and spring onions while the pork cooks, not after the pan is smoking like a distress flare.","Add the vegetables and stir-fry for 2–3 minutes so they stay crisp.","Mix soy, honey, sesame oil, ginger and chilli flakes, then pour it in and let it bubble until glossy.","Toss through noodles and finish with spring onions. Serve immediately; noodles wait for absolutely nobody."]},
  {name:"Roast Chicken Thigh Butternut Curry",category:"Family",tags:["Family","Batch Cook"],time:95,cost:2.46,protein:40,calories:721,difficulty:"Easy",score:9.7,emoji:"🍛",image:"/recipes/roast-chicken-thigh-butternut-curry.jpg",blurb:"Roast chicken thighs, squash, potatoes and a rich coconut curry sauce. The tray does the heavy lifting for once.",verdict:"A deep, proper curry with roasted edges and none of the watery jar-sauce nonsense.",ingredients:["2kg chicken thighs, bone-in and skin-on","1 butternut squash","3 potatoes","2 onions","3 peppers","2 tbsp olive oil","2 tsp salt","½ tsp black pepper","1½ tbsp plain flour","3 tbsp mild curry powder","1½ tsp turmeric","1½ tsp cumin","1 tbsp ground coriander","1½ tsp garam masala","1 tbsp butter","800ml coconut milk","800g chopped tomatoes","Rice to serve"],steps:["Heat the oven to 180°C fan. Toss squash, potatoes, onions and peppers with oil, salt and pepper in a large roasting tin. Spread the veg out; a deep pile stays wet instead of roasting.","Sit the chicken thighs on top, skin-side up, and roast for about an hour until the skin is golden and the vegetables are tender. Do not hide the chicken under the veg like it has done something wrong.","While it roasts, melt butter with oil in a large pan, stir in flour and every spice, and cook for 1–2 minutes. Raw curry powder tastes like dusty regret.","Whisk in coconut milk and chopped tomatoes until smooth, then simmer gently. Break up the spice paste now; gritty sauce will not fix itself.","Pull the cooked chicken from the bones and shred all the meat into the sauce. Check for small bones before returning the meat; crunchy curry is not what we are making.","Stir in the roasted vegetables and simmer 15–20 minutes until rich and thick. Stir occasionally so the bottom does not catch, then serve with rice; burnt sauce is a miserable reward for all that roasting."]},
  {name:"Creamy Garlic Chicken Spaghetti",category:"Family",tags:["Family","Quick"],time:35,cost:1.92,protein:35,calories:728,difficulty:"Easy",score:9.5,emoji:"🍝",image:"/recipes/creamy-garlic-chicken-spaghetti.jpg",blurb:"Garlicky chicken spaghetti with crispy garlic-bread crumbs. Creamy comfort without pretending to be delicate.",verdict:"Every forkful is garlic, cream and comfort. Bad breath is a small price to pay.",ingredients:["1kg chicken legs","150ml double cream","2 garlic bread baguettes","300g spaghetti","1 garlic bulb","1 tbsp oil","Salt and black pepper","1 tsp garlic granules","1 tsp dried parsley"],steps:["Remove the meat from the chicken legs and dice it evenly. Keep your fingers out of the way; dinner is not worth a trip to A&E.","Get one garlic baguette baking and cook the spaghetti in salted water according to the packet. Save some pasta water before draining; creamy spaghetti needs loosening, not a puddle of extra cream.","Fry the chicken in a little oil with salt, pepper, garlic granules and parsley until cooked through and golden. Give the chicken room in the pan; piling it up only produces steam.","Add 5–6 minced garlic cloves and cook for 30 seconds. Any longer and you have burnt bitterness for garnish.","Pour in the cream, add the drained spaghetti and toss until every strand is coated. Loosen with a splash of pasta water if it looks tight.","Blitz the ends from the cooked garlic baguette into crumbs, toast them until golden and scatter over the pasta with slices of the remaining bread."]},
  {name:"Slow Cooker Sweet Potato Chilli",category:"Budget",tags:["Budget","Batch Cook","High Protein"],time:250,cost:1.86,protein:34,calories:612,difficulty:"Idiot-proof",score:9.2,emoji:"🌶️",image:"/recipes/slow-cooker-sweet-potato-chilli.jpg",blurb:"Beef, sweet potato, beans and mushrooms doing all the work while you get on with something else.",verdict:"Chuck it in, leave it alone, come back to a proper chilli. This is the dream.",ingredients:["500g 5% beef mince","390g kidney beans in chilli sauce","850g sweet potato","150g sweetcorn","1 chilli con carne seasoning packet","400g chopped tomatoes","250g mushrooms","80g reduced-fat cheddar","Fresh coriander","Salt and black pepper"],steps:["Dice the sweet potato into even chunks. Random boulders take forever and then somehow stay raw in the middle.","Add everything except the cheese and coriander to the slow cooker, season with salt and pepper and sprinkle over the chilli seasoning. Break up the mince as you stir; one enormous beef lump is not chilli.","Stir until properly combined. Brown the mince first if you want extra depth, but the slow cooker will still save your evening either way.","Cook on high for 4 hours or low for 7–8 hours until the sweet potato is tender and the chilli is thick. Check a big chunk with a fork; hard potato does not get a pass because the clock says dinner.","Taste before serving. The packet does not know how much salt your tomatoes needed.","Divide into bowls, top with cheddar and coriander if you are feeling fancy, then get stuck in."]},
  {name:"Spicy Sausage Rigatoni",category:"Family",tags:["Family","Quick"],time:35,cost:2.06,protein:33,calories:715,difficulty:"Easy",score:9.5,emoji:"🍝",image:"/recipes/spicy-sausage-rigatoni.jpg",blurb:"Crisp sausage, chilli, mushroom and a creamy tomato sauce that clings to every tube of rigatoni.",verdict:"Spicy, creamy and deeply unfair on anyone who thought pasta needed to be boring.",ingredients:["300g rigatoni","8 pork sausages","20g butter","1 red onion","150g mushrooms","1 tbsp chilli flakes","1 tsp chilli powder","1 tsp mixed herbs","1 tsp smoked paprika","2 tbsp garlic","2 tbsp tomato purée","500ml passata","200ml pasta water","2 tbsp crème fraîche","50g parmesan","Fresh parsley","Salt and black pepper"],steps:["Cook the rigatoni in salted boiling water and save two ladles of pasta water before draining. That starchy water is not optional decoration.","Fry the sausage meat over medium-high heat until crisp and golden, then lift it out before it overcooks.","Melt butter in the same pan and soften onion for 2–3 minutes. Add chilli flakes, chilli powder, garlic and tomato purée, stirring until the purée darkens.","Add mushrooms, return the sausage and stir through paprika, herbs, salt and pepper. Toss thoroughly; the spices belong throughout the pan, not on one mushroom.","Pour in passata and pasta water, simmer for a couple of minutes, then stir in parmesan and crème fraîche over a lower heat.","Toss through rigatoni until coated, finish with parsley and more parmesan. If you can still see a puddle of sauce, keep tossing."]},
  {name:"One-Pan Creamy Tomato Pappardelle",category:"Vegetarian",tags:["Vegetarian","One Pan"],time:25,cost:1.74,protein:19,calories:642,difficulty:"Easy",score:9.3,emoji:"🍅",image:"/recipes/one-pan-creamy-tomato-pappardelle.jpg",blurb:"Wide ribbons of pappardelle, cherry tomatoes, spinach and cream all cooked in one pan. Minimal washing-up, maximum sauce.",verdict:"Silky, garlicky, ridiculously easy. Add chicken or sausage if you want, but it holds its own without either.",ingredients:["225g pappardelle nests","280g cherry tomatoes","1 small red onion","2 handfuls spinach","6 garlic cloves","170g tomato paste","1 tsp oregano","1 tsp dried basil","1 tsp dried parsley","½ tsp chilli flakes","1 tsp salt","1 tsp black pepper","Zest of 1 lemon","3 tbsp olive oil","240ml double cream","600ml vegetable stock","Fresh basil","Parmesan"],steps:["Put the pappardelle, tomatoes, onion, spinach and garlic into a wide lidded pan. Keep the nests reasonably separate or they will weld together.","Scatter over oregano, basil, parsley, chilli flakes, salt, pepper and lemon zest, then dot the tomato paste across the top. Small blobs dissolve as you stir; one huge red lump takes far more persuasion.","Pour in olive oil, cream and stock, bring to a gentle simmer, cover and cook for 10 minutes. Keep it gentle; cream plastered up the sides of the pan is not progress.","Stir every couple of minutes so the pasta separates and the tomato paste melts into the sauce instead of sitting there in red lumps.","Once the pasta is tender and the sauce has thickened, taste and adjust seasoning. Cream and tomato need salt or they taste like a compromise.","Finish with torn basil and parmesan, then serve immediately while the sauce is silky rather than gluey."]}
  ,{"name":"BBQ Chicken Pasta Bake","category":"Family","tags":["Family","High Protein"],"time":65,"cost":2.69,"protein":54,"calories":692,"difficulty":"Easy","score":9.6,"emoji":"🍝","image":"/recipes/bbq-chicken-pasta-bake.jpg","blurb":"One dish of BBQ chicken, creamy tomato pasta and molten mozzarella. Conveniently built for anyone who hates washing up.","verdict":"A hands-off pasta bake that does not taste like you gave up halfway through.","ingredients":["200g dried pasta","600g diced chicken breast","80g grated mozzarella","1 onion, diced","2 peppers, diced","200g low-fat cream cheese","1 BBQ seasoning packet","400g chopped tomatoes","50g BBQ sauce","4 tsp lazy garlic","100ml water","Salt and black pepper"],"steps":["Heat the oven to 190°C first. Waiting for it later is not part of the recipe.","Dice the chicken, onion and peppers evenly; random boulders do not cook at the same speed.","Add everything except the mozzarella and the measured water to a large ovenproof dish, including the dry pasta. The pasta cooks in the sauce; boiling it first just guarantees mush.","Rinse the tomato tin with 100ml water and tip it in. That last bit is flavour, not waste.","Season and stir until the cream cheese is spread through instead of sitting there in one tragic lump.","Cover with foil and bake for 45 minutes so the pasta steams properly rather than staying crunchy out of spite.","Remove the foil, top with mozzarella and bake for 5 more minutes until melted and starting to colour. If it needs another minute, watch it; burnt cheese is not a crispy topping.","Rest for 5–10 minutes so it thickens. Dig in early and it is tomato soup with ambition."]}
  ,{"name":"Peri Peri Chicken Rice Bake","category":"Family","tags":["Family","High Protein"],"time":55,"cost":2.46,"protein":52,"calories":646,"difficulty":"Easy","score":9.5,"emoji":"🍚","image":"/recipes/peri-peri-chicken-rice-bake.jpg","blurb":"Spicy peri-peri chicken and tomato rice baked in one dish, with jalapeños for people who have stopped pretending mild is exciting.","verdict":"Big heat, one dish and a rice bake with actual personality.","ingredients":["250g arborio rice","600g diced chicken breast","400g chopped tomatoes","2 peppers, diced","1 onion, diced","25g peri peri seasoning","100ml peri peri sauce","1 chicken stock cube","450ml boiling water","85g jalapeños, optional","Salt and black pepper"],"steps":["Heat the oven to 190°C. A cold oven is a delay tactic, not a method.","Put the rice, chicken, tomatoes, peppers, onion, peri-peri seasoning, sauce and jalapeños in a large ovenproof dish.","Dissolve the stock cube in boiling water, pour it in and stir properly so the spice does not all gather in one rude mouthful.","Season, level the dish and bake uncovered for 45 minutes. Spread the rice evenly; a mound above the liquid stays crunchy.","Stir once halfway through; leaving the rice untouched is how you get a crunchy little rebellion at the edges.","Check the chicken is cooked and the rice is tender. If it needs it, add a splash of hot water and give it 5 more minutes.","Rest for 5–10 minutes so the rice drinks up the sauce rather than collapsing across the plate."]}
  ,{"name":"Slow Cooker Sweet Chilli Beef Noodles","category":"Family","tags":["Family","Slow Cooker","High Protein"],"time":260,"cost":2.64,"protein":43,"calories":684,"difficulty":"Easy","score":9.4,"emoji":"🍜","image":"/recipes/slow-cooker-sweet-chilli-beef-noodles.jpg","blurb":"Tender beef in sticky honey, soy and sweet-chilli sauce with noodles added at the end, because nobody asked for noodle porridge.","verdict":"Proof that a slow cooker can do more than beige stew.","ingredients":["400g lean diced beef","2 peppers, sliced","1 onion, sliced","420g cooked egg noodles","40g sweet chilli sauce","30ml light soy sauce","40g runny honey","30g sriracha","50g tomato ketchup","20g easy garlic","Salt and black pepper","Fresh chilli, sesame seeds and coriander, optional"],"steps":["Add beef, sweet chilli, soy, honey, sriracha, ketchup and garlic to the slow cooker. Keep the vegetables and noodles out; they are not built for a six-hour bath.","Season and stir until every piece is coated. Turn the pieces through the mixture; seasoning only the top ones is not finishing the job. Patchy sauce is just blandness pretending to be confident.","Cook on high for 4 hours or low for 6–8 hours until the beef pulls apart easily with a fork. Leave the lid on; releasing the heat every ten minutes only delays the tender bit.","Add the onion and peppers with 20 minutes left so they keep some bite instead of becoming wallpaper.","Cook the noodles to the packet instructions just before serving. Wet socks have more dignity than overcooked noodles.","Remove the lid, fold in the drained noodles and taste. Adjust seasoning now, not silently at the table.","Finish with chilli, sesame and coriander if using, then serve before the noodles swallow all your sauce."]}
  ,{"name":"Chilli Garlic Prawn Skewers","category":"Quick","tags":["Quick","High Protein","Summer"],"time":18,"cost":2.38,"protein":22,"calories":248,"difficulty":"Easy","score":9.3,"emoji":"🍤","image":"/recipes/chilli-garlic-prawn-skewers.jpg","blurb":"Jumbo prawns punched up with garlic, lemon, chilli and smoked paprika. Tiny cooking time, zero room for rubbery nonsense.","verdict":"Bright, smoky and gone in minutes if you have any sense.","ingredients":["170g raw jumbo king prawns","1 lemon","3 garlic cloves, finely chopped","Fresh parsley, finely chopped","1 red chilli, deseeded and finely chopped","1 tsp smoked paprika","5 tbsp olive oil","Salt"],"steps":["Mix parsley, chilli, garlic, oil, lemon juice, paprika and salt in a bowl. Chop the garlic finely; big raw chunks do not count as bold flavour.","Coat the prawns with half the marinade. Do not leave them in lemon all day unless chewy prawns are your hobby.","Thread them onto skewers without crushing them into a seafood traffic jam.","Cook on a medium barbecue, griddle or grill for 2–3 minutes per side, or air fry at 180°C for 5–6 minutes, turning halfway. Watch the prawns rather than wandering off; they cook fast.","Turn and baste with clean marinade until pink and opaque. Charred garlic is bitter, not brave.","Take them off immediately when cooked; prawns go from juicy to pencil eraser in seconds.","Spoon over the remaining marinade and serve straight away with whatever you fancy."]}
  ,{"name":"Cheesy Leek Gratin","category":"Vegetarian","tags":["Vegetarian","Family"],"time":50,"cost":2.18,"protein":19,"calories":472,"difficulty":"Easy","score":9.4,"emoji":"🧀","image":"/recipes/cheesy-leek-gratin.jpg","blurb":"Silky leeks and shallots in a Dijon cheese sauce under a crisp Gruyère crumb. Vegetables with a far better plan than boiling.","verdict":"The side dish that will quietly become the main event.","ingredients":["4 large leeks, whites only","4 shallots, sliced","4 garlic cloves, finely chopped","1 tsp fresh thyme leaves","50g butter","150ml white wine","35g plain flour","600ml milk","1 tbsp Dijon mustard","1 tsp grated nutmeg","100g mature cheddar, grated","100g Gruyère, grated","Breadcrumbs","Salt and black pepper"],"steps":["Heat the oven to 200°C. Trim and rinse the leeks well; grit is not a rustic garnish.","Melt butter in a wide pan and add leeks, shallots, garlic, salt and pepper. Give them space or they steam into misery.","Cook for 8–10 minutes until soft, then add thyme. Stir from the bottom; scorched leeks make the entire cheese sauce bitter.","Stir in the flour and cook for 2 minutes. Raw flour tastes like you have lost control of the kitchen.","Pour in the wine, reduce for a minute, then add milk in three stages while stirring. Smooth out each addition before the next; tipping it all in at once is how you earn lumps.","When it coats a spoon, stir in Dijon, nutmeg, cheddar and most of the Gruyère off the heat. Do not boil it into cheese gravel.","Tip into a dish, top with breadcrumbs, remaining Gruyère and pepper, then bake for 20 minutes until deeply golden.","Rest for 5 minutes; molten cheese has no sympathy for your mouth."]}
  ,{"name":"Spicy Meatball Rigatoni Bake","category":"Family","tags":["Family","High Protein"],"time":75,"cost":2.74,"protein":40,"calories":731,"difficulty":"Medium","score":9.7,"emoji":"🍝","image":"/recipes/spicy-meatball-rigatoni-bake.jpg","blurb":"Beef-and-sausage meatballs, slow tomato sauce, rigatoni and enough mozzarella to make the dish actively dangerous straight from the oven.","verdict":"A proper bubbling meatball bake, not a jar of sauce pretending it tried.","ingredients":["250g beef mince","250g sausage meat","2 eggs","60g panko breadcrumbs","5 garlic cloves, divided","50g Parmigiano Reggiano, grated","50ml milk","Fresh flat-leaf parsley, chopped","2 tbsp chilli flakes","Olive oil","1 red chilli, sliced","Fresh basil","4 tbsp tomato paste","690g passata","200–250g mezzi rigatoni","Fresh mozzarella","Salt and black pepper"],"steps":["Mix beef, sausage meat, eggs, panko, 2 garlic cloves, Parmesan, milk, parsley, chilli, salt and pepper. Overmix it and the meatballs will bounce.","Chill the rolled meatballs for 20 minutes so they hold together like they have some self-respect.","Brown them all over in olive oil, then remove. Build colour, not dry cannonballs.","Cook sliced garlic, chilli and basil briefly, then cook out the tomato paste for 2 minutes. Keep the garlic moving so the sauce tastes rich, not burnt.","Add passata and simmer gently for 45 minutes so it tastes like sauce, not tomato water.","Return meatballs for the last 10 minutes until cooked through, then remove the spent basil. Check a meatball centre; browned outside is not proof the mince is cooked.","Cook rigatoni just shy of al dente, toss it through the sauce and taste before pretending it is seasoned.","Bake in a dish with meatballs, mozzarella and Parmesan at 220°C for 20–25 minutes until bubbling and golden.","Rest for 5 minutes before demolishing it; the cheese is not ready to negotiate."]}
  ,{"name":"Charred Chicken Tikka Masala","category":"Family","tags":["Family","High Protein","Fakeaway"],"time":70,"cost":3.12,"protein":46,"calories":658,"difficulty":"Medium","score":9.9,"emoji":"🍛","image":"/recipes/charred-chicken-tikka-masala.jpg","blurb":"Charred yoghurt-spiced chicken thighs in a silky cashew, tomato, butter and cream sauce. Takeaway-level comfort without the app refresh.","verdict":"Deep, creamy, spicy and worth every pan you will have to wash.","ingredients":["6 boneless skinless chicken thighs","8 tbsp natural yoghurt","10 garlic cloves, divided","20g fresh ginger, divided","½ lemon, juiced","2 tsp salt","1 tsp ground cumin","½ tsp ground turmeric","1½ tsp ground coriander","1 green chilli, minced","80g ghee or butter","1 cinnamon stick","4 cardamom pods","1 tsp cumin seeds","4 cloves","2 onions, finely sliced","1 tbsp tomato purée","80g cashews, soaked for 2 hours","1½ tsp chilli powder","2 tsp ground cumin","½ tsp ground fenugreek","2 tsp garam masala","400g chopped tomatoes","150ml double cream","2½ tbsp dried fenugreek leaves","Extra butter","Fresh coriander, chopped"],"steps":["Mix chicken with yoghurt, 6 garlic cloves, half the ginger, lemon, salt, cumin, turmeric, coriander and green chilli. Marinate for at least 4 hours; flavour needs time, not a pep talk.","Grill the chicken under fierce heat until charred at the edges. Get colour on the outside without drying it out; it still has ten minutes in the sauce to finish.","Heat the ghee, add cinnamon, cardamom, cumin seeds and cloves and toast for one minute. Keep them moving; burnt whole spices make bitter sauce.","Brown the onions properly. Pale onions make pale, forgettable sauce.","Add tomato purée, remaining garlic and ginger, then the ground spices. Stir for 2–3 minutes over a moderate heat; spice stuck and burnt to the pan is not extra depth.","Add cashews and tomatoes, simmer for 20 minutes, then remove the whole spices before somebody finds one with their teeth.","Stir in cream and a pinch of dried fenugreek, then blend smooth. Blend until the cashews are smooth; gritty bits will not disappear because the sauce smells good.","Return chicken with garam masala and remaining fenugreek, then simmer for 10 minutes until cooked through. Keep it gentle; a rolling boil tightens the chicken and splits the cream.","Finish with butter, cream, chilli and coriander. Serve hot and enjoy beating takeaway without pretending it was effortless."]}

  ,{name:"Garlic Chilli Chicken Noodles",category:"Quick",tags:["Quick","High Protein"],time:30,cost:2.34,protein:38,calories:628,difficulty:"Easy",score:9.5,emoji:"🍜",image:"/recipes/garlic-chilli-chicken-noodles.jpg",blurb:"Glossy noodles, golden chicken, kale and enough garlic to wake a whole street up.",verdict:"Fast, fiery and properly savoury. Takeaway has had a decent run.",ingredients:["410g cooked egg noodles","300g boneless chicken thighs","5 garlic cloves, sliced","100g kale","3 eggs","1 red chilli, sliced","4 tbsp dark soy sauce","2 tbsp light soy sauce","2 tsp rice vinegar","2 tsp honey","Fresh coriander","Oil","White pepper"],steps:["Slice the chicken and coat it with 1 tablespoon dark soy and a pinch of white pepper. Give it ten minutes; flavour does not arrive by magic.","Mix the remaining soy, vinegar and honey in a cup before the pan gets hot. Measuring sticky honey mid-chaos is how people burn dinner.","Heat a large pan until properly fierce, then sear the chicken for 2 minutes per side without poking it every three seconds.","Push the chicken aside, add a little oil and scramble the eggs into soft big ribbons. Tiny dry egg crumbs are not a victory.","Add garlic and chilli for 30 seconds, then toss in the noodles and sauce until everything turns dark and glossy. Keep tossing; sweet sauce left still in a hot pan burns.","Throw in the kale with a splash of water, toss for one minute until wilted, then finish with coriander and eat while the noodles still have some fight."]},
  {name:"Chilli Chicken Burger with Mango Slaw",category:"Fakeaway",tags:["Fakeaway","High Protein"],time:30,cost:2.58,protein:42,calories:612,difficulty:"Easy",score:9.4,emoji:"🍔",image:"/recipes/chilli-chicken-burger-mango-slaw.jpg",blurb:"Juicy spiced chicken, creamy avocado and sharp mango slaw in a proper burger bun.",verdict:"Sweet heat, crunch and no sad dry chicken pretending it is a burger.",ingredients:["4 chicken thigh fillets","4 brioche buns","1 tsp chilli flakes","1 tsp garlic granules","1 tsp smoked paprika","½ tsp ground cumin","½ mango, sliced","¼ red cabbage, shredded","½ red onion, sliced","1 lime","1 avocado","Iceberg lettuce","Fresh coriander","Oil","Salt and black pepper"],steps:["Heat a griddle or frying pan over medium-high heat. Cold chicken on a timid pan is a direct route to sadness.","Toss the thighs with chilli, garlic, paprika, cumin, oil, salt and pepper until every bit is dressed properly.","Mix mango, cabbage, onion, coriander and lime juice for the slaw. It should be sharp enough to cut through the rich chicken, without drowning it. A little lime sharpens the slaw; a puddle soaks the bun.","Cook chicken for 5–6 minutes per side until charred at the edges and cooked through, then rest it for 3 minutes because it is not a sprint.","Mash avocado with salt and lime, shred the lettuce and toast the buns cut-side down until golden. Toast the cut surfaces; a soggy bun wastes the crisp slaw you just made.","Build avocado, lettuce, chicken and slaw into each bun. Press lightly and serve before the slaw turns the whole thing into a soggy crime scene."]},
  {name:"Cornflake Air Fryer Chicken Salad",category:"Air Fryer",tags:["Air Fryer","High Protein"],time:35,cost:2.72,protein:44,calories:558,difficulty:"Easy",score:9.3,emoji:"🥗",image:"/recipes/cornflake-air-fryer-chicken-salad.jpg",blurb:"Crunchy cornflake chicken over a proper loaded salad with charred corn, feta and sriracha-lime dressing.",verdict:"A salad with a crunch loud enough to shut up anyone calling it boring.",ingredients:["4 chicken breasts","70g cornflakes, crushed","40g mixed seeds","3 tbsp mayonnaise","1 tbsp sriracha","2 limes","2 corn cobs","2 celery sticks, sliced","2 little gem lettuces","2 spring onions, sliced","80g feta","Salt and black pepper","Oil spray"],steps:["Heat the air fryer to 200°C. Waiting until the chicken is coated is just standing around with a problem.","Brush chicken lightly with mayo, then press it into crushed cornflakes and seeds until the coating actually sticks. Press firmly; loose crumbs just decorate the basket.","Spray the basket, add chicken with space around each piece and cook for 10 minutes; turn and cook 6–8 minutes more until crisp and cooked through.","Char the corn under a hot grill, turning it until the kernels pick up colour. Turn it for browned patches all round; scorching one side while the other stays raw is not charring.","Whisk mayo, sriracha and lime juice into a dressing, loosening it with a splash of water if it is too thick to behave.","Toss lettuce, celery, spring onion, corn and feta with dressing, then slice the chicken on top. Serve immediately before the coating loses its nerve."]},
  {name:"Sweet Soy Cod with Sriracha Broccoli",category:"High Protein",tags:["High Protein","Quick"],time:28,cost:3.46,protein:46,calories:492,difficulty:"Easy",score:9.6,emoji:"🐟",image:"/recipes/sweet-soy-cod-sriracha-broccoli.jpg",blurb:"Sticky five-spice cod with hot sriracha broccoli and a peanut crunch that knows exactly what it is doing.",verdict:"Fish cooked with purpose, not steamed into silence.",ingredients:["2 cod loins","2 tbsp light soy sauce","1 tbsp soft brown sugar","1 tsp five-spice","10g fresh ginger, grated","250g tenderstem broccoli","1 tbsp mayonnaise","1 tbsp sriracha","1 tbsp lemon juice","1 tbsp roasted peanuts, crushed","1 tsp sesame oil","1 tsp chilli oil","Oil","Salt"],steps:["Heat the oven to 220°C and line a tray. Cod deserves a hot start, not a leisurely spa day.","Mix soy, sugar, five-spice and ginger until the sugar dissolves, then brush half over the cod. Save a little soy for the broccoli dressing; it cannot all end up on the fish.","Roast for 12–15 minutes, basting once halfway, until the fish flakes and the edges go sticky. Do not keep basting every minute like you have nowhere else to be.","Boil the broccoli for 2 minutes until bright green, then drain it before it goes limp and ashamed.","Stir mayo, sriracha, soy and lemon into a punchy dressing, then toss through the warm broccoli.","Plate the cod with broccoli and finish with peanuts, sesame oil and chilli oil. Use rice if you want, but this does not need rescuing."]},
  {name:"Spicy Mushroom Walnut Ragù",category:"Vegetarian",tags:["Vegetarian","Family"],time:60,cost:1.92,protein:18,calories:644,difficulty:"Easy",score:9.2,emoji:"🍝",image:"/recipes/spicy-mushroom-ragu-pasta.jpg",blurb:"Roasted mushrooms and walnuts make a thick, spicy tomato ragù that does not miss the meat.",verdict:"Deep, rich and completely vegetarian without pretending to be a salad.",ingredients:["500g chestnut mushrooms","100g walnuts","400g pasta","1 onion, diced","3 garlic cloves, chopped","2 celery sticks, diced","400g chopped tomatoes","2 tbsp tomato purée","1 vegetable stock cube","1 tsp harissa","40g parmesan","Olive oil","Salt and black pepper"],steps:["Heat the oven to 220°C. Chop mushrooms and walnuts roughly; turning them into dust makes the sauce taste like potting compost.","Roast mushrooms on a tray with oil, salt and pepper for 15 minutes, then add walnuts for 5 more until everything smells serious.","Cook onion and celery in oil for 8 minutes until softened, then add garlic for 30 seconds. Burn it and start explaining yourself to the bin.","Stir in tomato purée and harissa for 2 minutes, then add tomatoes, stock cube and a splash of water.","Fold in the roasted mushrooms and walnuts and simmer for 15 minutes until thick enough to cling to a spoon rather than flee from it.","Cook pasta until al dente, toss through the ragù with Parmesan and serve hot. If it looks dry, use pasta water—not panic."]},
  {name:"Tuna Melt Enchiladas",category:"Family",tags:["Family","Budget"],time:45,cost:1.88,protein:31,calories:654,difficulty:"Easy",score:9.1,emoji:"🌯",image:"/recipes/tuna-melt-enchiladas.jpg",blurb:"Tuna, sweetcorn and roasted pepper wrapped in tortillas, drowned in tomato sauce and melted mozzarella.",verdict:"The tuna bake nobody saw coming, and nobody will leave behind.",ingredients:["3 tins tuna in spring water","6 tortillas","1 tin sweetcorn","1 red onion, diced","2 garlic cloves","1 roasted red pepper, chopped","400g chopped tomatoes","150g mozzarella","100g sour cream","Fresh coriander","1 red chilli, sliced","Olive oil","Salt and black pepper"],steps:["Heat the oven to 200°C. Heat it before filling the tortillas; leaving them sitting in cold tomato sauce is how the bottoms get soggy.","Drain tuna and sweetcorn well, then mix with half the sour cream, half the mozzarella, roasted pepper, coriander, salt and pepper. Drain means drain; tuna water makes a soggy filling.","Fill the tortillas and roll them tightly, seam-side down in a baking dish. Loose wraps unravel faster than bad plans.","Cook onion and garlic in oil for 3 minutes, add tomatoes and simmer 5 minutes before blending or crushing into a quick sauce. Soften the onion before adding tomatoes; crunchy onion does not belong in this sauce.","Pour sauce over the tortillas, dot with remaining sour cream and cover with mozzarella. Spread the sauce to the exposed tortilla edges so they bake tender, not dry and brittle.","Bake for 20–25 minutes until bubbling and brown at the edges. Finish with chilli and coriander, then give the lava two minutes to calm down."]},
  {name:"Chilled Sweetcorn Gazpacho",category:"Vegetarian",tags:["Vegetarian","Summer"],time:25,cost:1.62,protein:11,calories:328,difficulty:"Easy",score:8.9,emoji:"🌽",image:"/recipes/chilled-sweetcorn-gazpacho.jpg",blurb:"Cold, silky sweetcorn soup with tomato-cucumber crunch and frozen feta falling over the top like edible snow.",verdict:"Summer in a bowl, provided you remember to freeze the feta before pretending this was spontaneous.",ingredients:["4 corn cobs","1 cucumber","2 yellow peppers","300g tomatoes","1 lemon","2 tbsp apple cider vinegar","4 tbsp olive oil","Fresh basil","150g feta, frozen overnight","Chilli flakes","Salt and black pepper","Ice cubes"],steps:["Freeze the feta the day before. You cannot grate a warm block into snow, no matter how confidently you shout at it.","Slice kernels from the corn, roughly chop half the cucumber and the peppers, then add them to a blender. Chop them small enough for the blades to work; a blender is not a wood chipper.","Blend with lemon zest, vinegar, olive oil, ice, salt and enough cold water to make it silky, not like yellow cement.","Taste it cold and adjust with lemon, salt or a pinch of sugar. Seasoning warm soup is one thing; this needs checking properly.","Dice tomatoes and the remaining cucumber, then toss with basil, olive oil, pepper and chilli flakes. Dice finely enough to sit on a spoon; enormous salad chunks are awkward on soup.","Pour into bowls, top with the salad and grate the frozen feta generously over. Do not use a cheese slice and call it a day."]},
  {name:"Sticky Curry Mango Chicken Traybake",category:"Family",tags:["Family","High Protein"],time:45,cost:2.68,protein:43,calories:661,difficulty:"Easy",score:9.5,emoji:"🍗",image:"/recipes/sticky-curry-mango-chicken-traybake.jpg",blurb:"Charred tikka-mango chicken with black bean lime rice, quick-pickled onion and sharp cabbage slaw.",verdict:"A traybake that actually earns its sticky edges.",ingredients:["8 boneless chicken thighs","3 tbsp tikka paste","2 tbsp mango chutney","1 mango, sliced","250g microwave rice","1 tin black beans","1 red onion, sliced","½ cabbage, shredded","2 limes","Fresh coriander","Olive oil","Salt and black pepper"],steps:["Heat the oven to 200°C. A traybake without a hot oven is just a pile of raw optimism.","Toss chicken with tikka paste, mango chutney, oil, salt and pepper, then roast for 18–20 minutes until cooked through.","Massage sliced onion with lime juice and salt, then leave it to pickle while you get on with the actual cooking.","Toss cabbage with more lime and a pinch of salt until it softens slightly. It is slaw, not a punishment.","Warm rice, fold through drained black beans, coriander and lime zest, and taste it before serving like a grown-up.","Add mango to the chicken tray and grill for 3–4 minutes until charred, then serve over rice with slaw and onion. Watch the grill closely; mango chutney goes from caramelised to black in a moment."]},
  {name:"Smoky Gammon Campfire Stew",category:"Budget",tags:["Budget","Slow Cooker","Batch Cook"],time:370,cost:1.74,protein:35,calories:466,difficulty:"Idiot-proof",score:9.5,emoji:"🥘",image:"/recipes/smoky-gammon-campfire-stew.jpg",blurb:"Tender gammon, beans and green peppers in a smoky tomato stew that earns every slow-cooker minute.",verdict:"Proper comfort food with no pastry lid pretending it is a pie.",ingredients:["600g gammon joint, trimmed","2 tins baked beans","400g chopped tomatoes","1 onion, diced","3 garlic cloves","2 tbsp tomato purée","2 tsp cumin","2 tsp sweet smoked paprika","½ tsp mild chilli powder","2 tbsp Worcestershire sauce","2 green peppers, diced"],steps:["Put gammon, beans, tomatoes, onion, garlic, purée, cumin, paprika, chilli and Worcestershire sauce in the slow cooker. Yes, all of it—this is one of those rare moments life is simple.","Cook on high for 6 hours or low for 8 until the gammon falls apart. Do not lift the lid every twenty minutes; steam escaping is not progress.","Lift out the gammon and shred it with two forks, removing excess fat. Pull it apart properly; huge chewy lumps defeat the point of slow-cooking it.","Microwave or fry the peppers for 3–4 minutes so they keep their colour and do not dissolve into swamp water.","Return gammon and peppers to the pot, stir hard and taste before adding salt—gammon and beans have already had plenty to say.","Serve with a jacket potato, rice or bread. Shred the gammon properly before serving; a giant chunk in one bowl and sauce in another is not portioning."]},
  {name:"Slow Cooker Honey BBQ Pulled Chicken",category:"Slow Cooker",tags:["Slow Cooker","Family","High Protein"],time:250,cost:2.26,protein:39,calories:522,difficulty:"Idiot-proof",score:9.3,emoji:"🍗",image:"/recipes/slow-cooker-honey-bbq-pulled-chicken.jpg",blurb:"Chicken cooked until it shreds in a sticky honey-barbecue sauce, ready for buns, wraps or a frankly massive jacket potato.",verdict:"Low effort, high reward and gloriously messy.",ingredients:["700g chicken thighs","180ml BBQ sauce","2 tbsp tomato ketchup","1 tbsp honey","1 tbsp cider vinegar","1 tsp mustard powder","1 tsp smoked paprika","1 tsp garlic granules","4 burger buns","200g coleslaw","Spring onions","Salt and black pepper"],steps:["Lay chicken thighs in the slow cooker. Do not bother browning them—this one is built to collapse, not pose for a magazine.","Whisk BBQ sauce, ketchup, honey, vinegar, mustard powder, paprika, garlic, salt and pepper, then pour it over. Coat every thigh; the top ones do not deserve all the sauce.","Cook on high for 3–4 hours or low for 5–6 until the chicken shreds easily with two forks. Test a thick piece; forcing apart half-cooked chicken is not shredding.","Lift chicken out, shred with two forks and remove any skin, gristle or excess fat. Shred the meat, not the chewy bits nobody wants to find in a bun.","If the sauce is thin, bubble it in a pan for 5 minutes until sticky, then return the chicken. Reduce the sauce before mixing the chicken back in; wet filling soaks through a bun in seconds.","Pile into toasted buns with coleslaw and spring onion. Use two hands and wear something you are not emotionally attached to."]},
  {name:"Slow Cooker Chicken Fajitas",category:"Slow Cooker",tags:["Slow Cooker","Family"],time:250,cost:2.12,protein:41,calories:608,difficulty:"Easy",score:9.2,emoji:"🌯",image:"/recipes/slow-cooker-chicken-fajitas.jpg",blurb:"Soft, spicy chicken, peppers and onion slow-cooked for lazy fajitas that still taste like you tried.",verdict:"Fajitas for people who cannot be bothered to stand over a pan. Fair enough.",ingredients:["650g chicken breast","3 peppers, sliced","1 red onion, sliced","1 tin sweetcorn","400g chopped tomatoes","2 tbsp fajita seasoning","1 tbsp tomato purée","8 tortillas","120g grated cheddar","1 lime","Salt and black pepper"],steps:["Add chicken, peppers, onion, sweetcorn, tomatoes, fajita seasoning and purée to the slow cooker. Keep the wraps out; they are not built for a four-hour sauna.","Season and stir until the spice is spread through, not sitting in a single red clump waiting to ruin someone’s bite.","Cook on high for 4 hours or low for 6–7 until the chicken pulls apart easily. Leave the lid on; checking it every few minutes only delays dinner.","Shred the chicken into the sauce and leave the lid off for 10 minutes if it looks too wet. Nobody wants soup in a tortilla.","Warm the tortillas and stir half the cheese through the filling so every wrap gets some melt.","Load, top with more cheese and squeeze over lime. Fold tightly unless you enjoy fajita wearing."]},
  {name:"Slow Cooker Red Lentil Dahl",category:"Vegetarian",tags:["Vegetarian","Slow Cooker","Budget"],time:250,cost:1.28,protein:20,calories:508,difficulty:"Idiot-proof",score:9.4,emoji:"🍛",image:"/recipes/slow-cooker-red-lentil-dahl.jpg",blurb:"Red lentils, tomatoes, coconut and spinach cooked into a thick, warmly spiced bowlful.",verdict:"Cheap, filling and far more exciting than the word lentil has any right to be.",ingredients:["300g red lentils","1 onion, diced","3 garlic cloves","15g ginger, grated","400g chopped tomatoes","400ml light coconut milk","700ml vegetable stock","1 tbsp curry powder","1 tsp turmeric","1 tsp cumin","150g spinach","1 lemon","Fresh coriander","Salt and black pepper"],steps:["Rinse the lentils until the water runs mostly clear. Skip this and enjoy explaining why your dahl looks murky.","Add lentils, onion, garlic, ginger, tomatoes, coconut milk, stock and spices to the slow cooker, then stir properly. Break up any spice clumps now; nobody wants a spoonful of dry curry powder.","Cook on high for 3–4 hours or low for 6–7 until the lentils are tender and the sauce is thick. Keep the lid on while they cook; the heat belongs in the pot, not wafting round the kitchen.","Stir hard to break down the lentils a little; it should look creamy, not like grains floating in a bath.","Fold in spinach until wilted, then add lemon juice, salt and pepper. Acid at the end stops it tasting flat.","Top with coriander and serve with naan or rice. It will thicken as it sits, because even dahl needs a minute to get itself together."]},
  {name:"Sticky Glazed Meatloaf",category:"Family",tags:["Family","Budget"],time:70,cost:2.06,protein:38,calories:628,difficulty:"Easy",score:9.2,emoji:"🥩",image:"/recipes/sticky-glazed-meatloaf.jpg",blurb:"Tender beef meatloaf with a sticky tomato glaze and a proper sliceable centre, not a dry brick.",verdict:"Comfort food with edges. Literally.",ingredients:["750g beef mince","1 onion, grated","2 garlic cloves","1 egg","80g breadcrumbs","100ml milk","1 tsp dried oregano","1 tsp smoked paprika","3 tbsp tomato ketchup","1 tbsp brown sugar","1 tbsp Worcestershire sauce","Salt and black pepper","Mashed potato and green beans to serve"],steps:["Heat the oven to 190°C and line a loaf tin. Grease it unless you want the first serving to become an archaeological dig.","Mix mince, onion, garlic, egg, breadcrumbs, milk, oregano, paprika, salt and pepper gently. Knead it to death and it will eat like a boxing glove.","Press into the tin and level the top so it cooks evenly instead of producing one dry hill and one raw bog.","Mix ketchup, sugar and Worcestershire sauce, then brush half over the loaf. Save the rest for the second coat; one early layer will not give the same sticky finish.","Bake for 45 minutes, brush with the remaining glaze and bake 10–15 minutes more until cooked through and sticky.","Rest for 10 minutes before slicing. Cut it hot and you will be serving mince rubble with confidence."]},
  {name:"Mexican Bean and Corn Salad",category:"Vegetarian",tags:["Vegetarian","Quick","Summer"],time:20,cost:1.56,protein:18,calories:478,difficulty:"Easy",score:9.0,emoji:"🥗",image:"/recipes/mexican-bean-corn-salad.jpg",blurb:"A big sharp bowl of black beans, charred corn, avocado and lime that actually feels like dinner.",verdict:"Colourful, filling and no sad leaf pile in sight.",ingredients:["1 tin black beans","1 tin sweetcorn","2 little gem lettuces","250g cherry tomatoes","1 avocado","½ red onion, sliced","1 lime","Fresh coriander","1 tsp ground cumin","1 tsp smoked paprika","2 tbsp Greek yoghurt","1 tbsp olive oil","Salt and black pepper"],steps:["Drain and rinse beans and sweetcorn properly. Tinned-water flavour is not part of Mexican cuisine.","Char the sweetcorn in a dry hot pan for 3–4 minutes until it catches at the edges. Drain it first or the pan will boil corn water instead of browning kernels.","Whisk yoghurt, lime juice, cumin, paprika, oil, salt and pepper into a smooth dressing. Taste it before pouring; a sharply dressed salad beats a bland bowl of good intentions.","Chop lettuce, tomatoes, avocado and onion into bite-sized pieces. Nobody can elegantly eat a whole lettuce leaf.","Toss everything with coriander and most of the dressing, keeping the avocado gentle so it does not become guacamole by accident.","Pile into bowls and drizzle the rest over the top. Eat soon; avocado has a shocking attitude about being left alone."]},
  {name:"Tuna Pasta Salad",category:"Quick",tags:["Quick","Budget"],time:18,cost:1.52,protein:29,calories:572,difficulty:"Easy",score:8.9,emoji:"🥗",image:"/recipes/tuna-pasta-salad.jpg",blurb:"Properly loaded tuna pasta with crunch, sweetcorn and a sharp lemon dressing—not the beige school-lunch version.",verdict:"Cold pasta with actual standards.",ingredients:["300g fusilli","2 tins tuna in spring water","1 tin sweetcorn","½ cucumber, diced","200g cherry tomatoes","½ red onion, diced","4 tbsp light mayonnaise","1 lemon","Fresh parsley","Salt and black pepper"],steps:["Boil the pasta in well-salted water until just tender. Pasta salad with mushy spirals is a punishment, not lunch.","Drain and rinse under cold water until cooled, then shake it dry. Waterlogged pasta dilutes everything it touches.","Drain the tuna and sweetcorn like you mean it; excess liquid makes the dressing slide straight off.","Mix mayonnaise, lemon juice, parsley, salt and pepper in a large bowl before adding anything else. Taste the dressing now; coating every spiral in bland mayo is not the aim.","Fold in pasta, tuna, corn, cucumber, tomatoes and onion until coated without smashing the tuna into wallpaper paste.","Chill for 15 minutes if you can, then taste again. Taste it chilled; cold food can need more seasoning, not more mayonnaise."]},
  {name:"Slow Cooker Sausage Casserole",category:"Slow Cooker",tags:["Slow Cooker","Family","Budget"],time:430,cost:1.86,protein:32,calories:610,difficulty:"Easy",score:9.3,emoji:"🌭",image:"/recipes/slow-cooker-sausage-casserole.jpg",blurb:"Sausages, butter beans and vegetables cooked into a thick tomato casserole that does not need a packet sauce to exist.",verdict:"A lazy-day classic with enough flavour to justify the waiting.",ingredients:["8 pork sausages","1 onion, diced","2 carrots, diced","2 peppers, diced","2 garlic cloves","400g chopped tomatoes","1 tin butter beans","500ml chicken stock","1 tbsp tomato purée","1 tsp mixed herbs","1 tsp smoked paprika","Fresh rosemary","Salt and black pepper"],steps:["Brown the sausages in a hot pan for 6–8 minutes. The slow cooker will cook them, but it cannot invent the flavour of a proper sear.","Put the sausages, onion, carrots, garlic, tomatoes, beans, stock, purée, herbs and paprika into the slow cooker, then stir until the tomato purée has disappeared into the stock. Scrape it through properly; a lump of purée is not a lucky bonus in someone's bowl.","Cook on high for 5–6 hours or low for 7–8 until the sauce is rich and the carrots are tender. Put the lid on and leave it alone; lifting it every ten minutes only adds cooking time.","Add the peppers for the final 45 minutes so they soften without turning to mush. They are meant to be in the casserole, not dissolved into it.","If the casserole is thin, leave the lid off for 20 minutes so steam can escape and the sauce can reduce. Do not throw in flour at the last minute; it will make the sauce claggy.","Stir through rosemary and black pepper, then serve with mash, bread or jackets while it is properly hot. Make enough space for the sauce; that is the best bit."]},
  {name:"Slow Cooker Salt and Pepper Chicken",category:"Slow Cooker",tags:["Slow Cooker","High Protein"],time:250,cost:2.38,protein:43,calories:438,difficulty:"Easy",score:9.4,emoji:"🍗",image:"/recipes/slow-cooker-salt-pepper-chicken.jpg",blurb:"Tender chicken, peppers and onion in a sticky garlic-and-black-pepper sauce with actual bite.",verdict:"All the salt-and-pepper takeaway energy, none of the greasy paper bag.",ingredients:["700g chicken thighs, diced","2 peppers, sliced","1 onion, sliced","3 garlic cloves","2 tbsp soy sauce","1 tbsp honey","1 tbsp rice vinegar","1 tsp sesame oil","1½ tsp cracked black pepper","½ tsp Chinese five-spice","2 spring onions","1 red chilli","Salt"],steps:["Add chicken, soy, honey, vinegar, sesame oil, black pepper, five-spice, garlic and a pinch of salt to the slow cooker. Black pepper is the point, so do not be shy now.","Stir until every chicken piece is coated. A dry corner is where flavour goes to die.","Cook on high for 3–4 hours or low for 5–6 until tender, leaving the peppers and onion out for now because they are better added later. Cook them for hours with the chicken and they lose all their texture.","Add peppers and onion for the final 30 minutes so they soften but keep some backbone.","Lift the lid and stir; if the sauce is loose, cook uncovered for 10–15 minutes until it turns sticky. Stir from the bottom; reducing sauce is not permission to burn it.","Top with spring onion and chilli and serve with rice. Taste first—soy sauce is salty enough without you freelancing."]},
  {name:"Cowboy Sausage and Bean Casserole",category:"Family",tags:["Family","Budget"],time:60,cost:1.64,protein:31,calories:682,difficulty:"Easy",score:9.1,emoji:"🥔",image:"/recipes/cowboy-sausage-bean-casserole.jpg",blurb:"Sausages and beans under a rough potato topping, baked until crisp at the edges and completely unapologetic.",verdict:"A cowboy casserole with more sense than a cowboy hat indoors.",ingredients:["8 pork sausages","600g potatoes, peeled","1 onion, diced","2 carrots, diced","1 tin baked beans","1 tin mixed beans","300ml beef stock","1 tbsp tomato purée","2 tsp mild curry powder","50g cheddar, grated","Oil","Salt and black pepper"],steps:["Heat the oven to 180°C and boil the potatoes until tender. Do not slice them tiny; we are making mash, not confetti.","Brown sausages until their skins are properly coloured, then set aside before they turn leathery.","Cook onion and carrots in the same pan for 5 minutes, then stir in beans, stock, purée and curry powder. Break up the purée as you stir; red lumps are not extra tomato flavour.","Simmer 10 minutes until saucy, then put sausages in a baking dish and pour the bean mix around them. Spread it evenly so the potato topping has a level surface, not a sausage obstacle course.","Mash potatoes with salt and pepper, spread over the top and fork it up so the ridges can actually crisp.","Scatter cheddar and bake 20 minutes until golden. Rest 5 minutes before serving; mashed potato is molten sabotage straight from the oven."]},
  {name:"Cheesy Tuna Pasta Bake",category:"Budget",tags:["Budget","Family"],time:45,cost:1.46,protein:29,calories:638,difficulty:"Easy",score:8.8,emoji:"🍝",image:"/recipes/cheesy-tuna-pasta-bake.jpg",blurb:"Tomato tuna pasta under a crisp cheddar lid—cheap, filling and nowhere near as dull as it sounds.",verdict:"The dependable weeknight bake, now with less beige resignation.",ingredients:["300g penne","2 tins tuna","1 onion, diced","2 garlic cloves","400g chopped tomatoes","1 tin sweetcorn","1 tsp dried oregano","100g mature cheddar, grated","1 tbsp olive oil","Salt and black pepper"],steps:["Heat the oven to 190°C and cook pasta two minutes short of the packet time. It has an oven date later, so stop overcooking it early.","Cook onion in oil for 4 minutes, add garlic for 30 seconds, then tip in tomatoes, oregano and pepper.","Simmer 8 minutes until the tomatoes lose that tinny raw edge, then fold in drained tuna and sweetcorn gently.","Mix sauce with pasta and taste it. Tomato and tuna without enough seasoning tastes like a Tuesday nobody wanted.","Tip into a baking dish, cover with cheddar and bake 18–20 minutes until golden and bubbling.","Rest for 5 minutes before serving. This is a bake, not a lava-dodge challenge."]},
  {name:"Chicken and Sweetcorn Pie",category:"Family",tags:["Family","Comfort Food"],time:55,cost:2.42,protein:38,calories:698,difficulty:"Easy",score:9.4,emoji:"🥧",image:"/recipes/chicken-sweetcorn-pie.jpg",blurb:"Creamy chicken, leek and sweetcorn under a crisp puff pastry lid. No pointless extras in the way.",verdict:"Golden pastry, proper filling and enough sauce to prove it is not a dry pie crime.",ingredients:["600g chicken breast, diced","1 leek, sliced","1 tin sweetcorn","25g butter","25g plain flour","350ml chicken stock","150ml milk","1 tsp Dijon mustard","1 puff pastry sheet","1 egg, beaten","Salt and black pepper"],steps:["Heat the oven to 200°C and fry chicken in a wide pan until just golden. It will finish in the sauce, so do not cremate it for confidence.","Add leek and butter, cook 5 minutes until soft, then stir in flour for one minute. Raw flour does not magically improve under pastry.","Gradually pour in stock and milk, stirring until smooth, then add mustard and sweetcorn. Add the liquid in stages; tipping it in at once only earns you flour lumps.","Simmer until thick enough to coat the chicken, season well and tip into a pie dish. Thin filling soaks the pastry from below; thicken it before building the pie.","Lay pastry over the filling, trim the edges and cut a steam hole. A sealed pie puffs up like it is hiding state secrets.","Brush with egg and bake 25–30 minutes until deeply golden. Leave it 10 minutes before serving or the filling will redecorate the plate."]},
  {name:"Blue Cheese and Bacon Pasta",category:"Family",tags:["Quick","Comfort Food"],time:25,cost:2.22,protein:30,calories:742,difficulty:"Easy",score:9.2,emoji:"🧀",image:"/recipes/blue-cheese-bacon-pasta.jpg",blurb:"Crisp bacon and bold blue cheese folded through creamy pasta with spinach and black pepper.",verdict:"Rich, salty and absolutely not here to be sensible.",ingredients:["300g tagliatelle","200g smoked bacon lardons","120g blue cheese","150ml double cream","100g spinach","1 garlic clove","Black pepper","Salt"],steps:["Boil tagliatelle in salted water until just al dente. Save a mug of pasta water because it is about to do more work than you expect.","Fry bacon lardons until crisp, then lift them out before they go from crunchy to charred gravel.","Lower the heat, add garlic for 20 seconds, then pour in cream. Keep it gentle; cream hates a panic boil.","Crumble in blue cheese and stir until melted, adding a splash of pasta water to make a glossy sauce instead of a greasy split mess.","Fold in spinach, pasta and most of the bacon until the leaves wilt and every ribbon is coated. Turn the pasta through the sauce; stirring the top alone leaves dry strands underneath.","Finish with remaining bacon and black pepper. Taste before salting—the bacon and cheese already bring plenty of salt. Add pepper freely, salt only after tasting."]},
  {name:"Creamy Chicken Potato Layer Bake",category:"Family",tags:["Family","Comfort Food"],time:75,cost:2.36,protein:42,calories:676,difficulty:"Easy",score:9.1,emoji:"🥔",image:"/recipes/creamy-chicken-potato-layer-bake.jpg",blurb:"Creamy chicken and thin potato layers baked under a golden cheddar top. All the comfort, none of the faff.",verdict:"A layered bake where every level has a job.",ingredients:["600g chicken breast, diced","900g potatoes, thinly sliced","1 onion, sliced","2 garlic cloves","250ml chicken stock","200ml single cream","150g mature cheddar, grated","1 tsp dried thyme","1 tbsp olive oil","Salt and black pepper"],steps:["Heat the oven to 190°C and oil a baking dish. Leaving it dry is an interesting way to glue dinner to the bottom.","Sear chicken for 3–4 minutes until it catches colour, then add onion and garlic for 2 minutes. Keep the pieces in one layer; crowded chicken sweats rather than browns.","Pour in stock and cream, add thyme, salt and pepper, then simmer 3 minutes until it just starts to thicken. Keep the heat moderate; boiling cream hard will not make a better sauce.","Layer half the potatoes in the dish, spoon over half the chicken sauce, then repeat. Keep the slices overlapping, not piled in one starchy mountain.","Cover tightly with foil and bake 40 minutes until potatoes are tender. You cannot rush undercooked potatoes with positive thinking.","Remove foil, scatter cheddar and bake 15 minutes more until golden. Rest 10 minutes so the layers stop sliding around like a landslide."]},
  {name:"Speedy Mackerel Spaghetti",category:"Quick",tags:["Quick","High Protein"],time:22,cost:2.46,protein:37,calories:618,difficulty:"Easy",score:9.3,emoji:"🍝",image:"/recipes/speedy-mackerel-spaghetti.jpg",blurb:"Smoky mackerel, lemon, capers and tomatoes tossed through spaghetti in the time it takes to choose a takeaway.",verdict:"Fast fish pasta with actual brightness, not a heavy cream blanket.",ingredients:["300g spaghetti","2 smoked mackerel fillets, flaked","250g cherry tomatoes","2 garlic cloves, sliced","1 lemon","2 tbsp capers","50g rocket","Fresh parsley","2 tbsp olive oil","Chilli flakes","Salt and black pepper"],steps:["Boil spaghetti in salty water and save a mug before draining. The pasta water is not optional; it is the difference between sauce and sad oil.","Cook tomatoes in olive oil for 4 minutes until they blister, then add garlic and chilli flakes for 30 seconds. Thirty seconds means watch the pan; burnt garlic takes the whole sauce with it.","Add capers, lemon zest and a splash of pasta water, scraping up the good bits rather than leaving them welded to the pan.","Toss through spaghetti until glossy, adding more pasta water if it looks dry. Do not drown it; we are not making broth.","Fold in mackerel gently at the end so it stays in proper flakes rather than becoming fish mush.","Add rocket, parsley, lemon juice and pepper, then serve fast. Fish waits for no one and neither does spaghetti."]},
  {name:"Scruffy Vegetable Lasagne",category:"Vegetarian",tags:["Vegetarian","Family","Batch Cook"],time:85,cost:2.14,protein:22,calories:648,difficulty:"Medium",score:9.4,emoji:"🍅",image:"/recipes/scruffy-vegetable-lasagne.jpg",blurb:"Roasted aubergine, courgette, peppers and spinach layered with tomato sauce, white sauce and bubbling mozzarella.",verdict:"Vegetable lasagne with enough depth to make meat feel unnecessary.",ingredients:["1 aubergine, diced","2 courgettes, diced","2 peppers, diced","1 onion, diced","3 garlic cloves","400g chopped tomatoes","500ml passata","150g spinach","9 lasagne sheets","40g butter","40g plain flour","500ml milk","200g mozzarella","40g parmesan","Olive oil","Salt and black pepper"],steps:["Heat the oven to 210°C, toss aubergine, courgette and peppers with oil, salt and pepper, then roast 25 minutes until caramelised. Pale roasted veg is just warm disappointment.","Cook onion and garlic in a pan, add tomatoes and passata, then simmer until thick enough to hold a spoon trail. Watery tomato sauce makes watery lasagne; reduce it before you start layering.","Melt butter, stir in flour for 2 minutes, then whisk in milk gradually until smooth. Lumps are not rustic; they are avoidable.","Stir spinach into the tomato sauce until wilted, then taste everything. Bland lasagne is a waste of several pans.","Layer sauce, sheets, white sauce and vegetables in a dish, repeating until you run out. Keep the final layer saucy or the sheets will crisp up out of spite.","Top with mozzarella and Parmesan, bake at 190°C for 35–40 minutes until bubbling, then rest 10 minutes before slicing. Let it set or accept lasagne landslide."]},
  {name:"Cajun Chicken Traybake",category:"Family",tags:["Family","High Protein"],time:50,cost:2.48,protein:45,calories:632,difficulty:"Easy",score:9.3,emoji:"🍗",image:"/recipes/cajun-chicken-traybake.jpg",blurb:"Cajun chicken thighs roasted with potatoes, sweetcorn, peppers and lime until the tray is full of proper colour.",verdict:"One tray, big flavour and no need to pretend dry chicken is healthy.",ingredients:["8 chicken thighs","700g baby potatoes, halved","2 corn cobs, cut into rounds","2 red peppers, chunked","1 red onion, chunked","2 tbsp Cajun seasoning","1 lime","2 tbsp olive oil","Fresh coriander","Salt and black pepper"],steps:["Heat the oven to 210°C and toss potatoes with oil, Cajun seasoning, salt and pepper on a large tray. Give them a 15-minute head start because potatoes do not cook by encouragement.","Add chicken thighs, corn, peppers and onion, turning everything through the spicy oil so no ingredient is sat there flavourless and offended.","Roast for 25–30 minutes until chicken is cooked through, potatoes are crisp and the corn has charred at the edges. Check a potato with a knife; hard middles need longer, not extra seasoning.","Turn the chicken once halfway if the tray is crowded. Move darker pieces away from the tray edges; one pale side and one burnt side is not evenly roasted.","Squeeze lime over the tray straight from the oven and scatter coriander to brighten the spicy coating. Use the juice, not seeds; they are not a garnish.","Rest 5 minutes, then serve straight from the tray if washing-up has already lost the argument."]}

] as const;
